      "writtenOn": "2024-12-26T22:29:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This also seems like a fairly weird encoding. Would it make sense to have dirty \u003d 4, aged \u003d 2, aged2 \u003d 1, and have aging do a right shift? You\u0027d have to be a bit more careful in interpreting the bits when you read the cards. But it feels more intuitive and faster, given that we\u0027re already trading bits for cheaper atomicity. (Which is probably the right trade-off for code size reasons, though it\u0027s not 100% clear.)",
      "parentUuid": "b41ae166_dada4d9c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "0f649e0289a9f84aa15b2f540070a66c8242ba44",
