      "lineNbr": 376,
      "author": {
        "id": 1258954
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-07T04:36:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Moving `NO_THREAD_SAFETY_ANALYSIS` to UpdateNonMovingPage() definintion in mark_compact.cc is not helping with supressing the compilation error. I tried.\n\nI added this because now I\u0027m calling card_table\u0027s Scan() in this function, which expects `heap_bitmap_lock_` to be exclusively acquired. I cannot do that as UpdateNonMovingPage can be called by mutators in SIGBUS handler.\n\nIt is puzzling that card-table\u0027s Scan() needs this lock exclusively. It seems to me that the idea is to avoid getting adding/deleting bitmap(s) to the heap. But that can be achieved by acquiring read-lock also, right?\n\nBut even if we relax the constraint, is it ok to acquire read-lock in a signal handler?\n\nHow about the gc-thread acquires the lock exclusively on the behalf of all threads calling UpdateNonMovingPage() and then we use NO_THREAD_SAFETY_ANALYSIS and explain that why it\u0027s safe if multiple threads call this function simultanesously?\n\nI\u0027ll wait for your suggestion before making any changes here.",
      "parentUuid": "6fdf268a_cb3d2a0f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 376,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 376,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "0f649e0289a9f84aa15b2f540070a66c8242ba44",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
